OL,2,V55555555CHELP FOR VICTIMS
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CIN CRIME CRACKDOWN
OL,4,B
OL,5, A tougher crackdown on criminals and a
OL,6, fairer deal for their victims is out-
OL,7, lined in a White Paper which will form
OL,8, the basis of a Criminal Justice Bill.
OL,10, It increases sentences - to life for
OL,11, having guns - and allows seizure of
OL,12, criminals' assets to compensate victims
OL,14, The right of a trial by jury may go in
OL,15, some minor cases and there will be
OL,16, easier extradition of alleged criminals
OL,18, Home Secretary Douglas Hurd said that
OL,19, the plans were part of a developing
OL,20, strategy, but Labour's Gerald Kaufman
OL,21, called the White Paper "a few patches
OL,22, of whitewash on a disgraceful record".
OL,23,F]DFrom 06-03-96 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
